                <pb facs="0539" n="2003" sameAs="frus:frus1951v06p2/pg2003"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">689.90D/11–2951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Afghanistan
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-12-29T19:33:00-05:00">December 29,
                            1951—7:33 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>206. Dept in accord desirability certain econ objectives and their relationship
                        Pak–Afghan relations advanced Embtel 260 Nov 29. However Dept questions
                    whether GOP wld be inclined actively to
                    cooperate in improvement Afghan econ position in absence demonstration good
                    faith GOA. Such demonstration not yet
                    forthcoming except decrease local press propaganda which not as significant as
                    radio propaganda that reaches Pak audience.</p>
                <p>
                    FYI re para 2 your memo conversation des 187 Dec
                    3 there are no funds available this FY for grant
                    aid to Kabul Kandahar highway project and Dept cannot now predict level MSP appropriation FY
                    1953. Hence in conversations with GOA Emb shld
                    carefully avoid statements that may lead Afghans expect more than Dept can
                    offer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
